  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "fieldDescription gives known negative fields none, otherwise focuses initialized fields, leaving unknown fields undefined. FieldBindings records this for each pattern pair. BindingTyped.variable preserves the type and requires a fresh name; .unpack requires same base class, declared class, a permutation of all field names, distinct/fresh destinations, and descriptions for every field. The display chooses declaration order and explicitly allows permutation afterward. It requires known direct statuses, not recursively Full views; the text makes precisely this distinction.",
  "limitations": [
    "Correspondence review compares prose, mathematics, definitions and theorem/example statements; Lean proof validity and command results are separate checks. Listing relevant source-context snapshots records definitions and assumptions consulted, not an audit of every tactic or unrelated declaration.",
    "Finite-map notation uses the documented distinct-key and well-formedness conventions. Raw Lean list representations also admit malformed values; no functional-lookup or preservation claim is made for those outside the stated premises."
